    pr_ref:  # c958
    description: "RESIDUAL of INV-bikaj, filed at its closure 2026-09-16 (dev 9c8c8165f0).\n\nINV-bikaj filed \"61 of 84 AnalysisRun passes produce 0 edges, 8 of them\nscanning 100+ files for nothing\". The instrumentation it asked for shipped\n(nodes_emitted / edges_emitted / silence_reason), and with it the population\nsplits. Measured on the hypergumbo self-analysis, 92 analysis_runs:\n\n  zero nodes AND edges          54/92\n    silence_reason=no_candidate_files   51   <- analysed 0 files, design-correct\n    silence_reason=unreported            3   <- analysed files, emitted nothing\n\nTHE POINT. The disclosure axis explains the 51 trivial cases, where the reason\nis derivable from files_analyzed=0 alone, and abstains on exactly the 3 cases\nthat are not trivially explainable. \"unreported\" means CANNOT DETERMINE. So the\nonly runs where a consumer actually needs to know why a pass was silent are the\nruns the mechanism declines to answer for.\n\nTHE THREE, all three being the entire >0-files zero-output cohort:\n\n  pass                      files  duration  silence_reason\n  graphql-resolver-linker   353    1915ms    unreported\n  message-queue-linker      353    1819ms    unreported\n  ipc-linker                8      9ms       unreported\n\nThe first two are also the whole of INV-bikaj's original \"scans 100+ files and\nemits nothing\" cohort at tip: 2 passes, 3734ms, 3.2% of the 115235ms total pass\ntime, down from the filed 8 passes / ~14s / 15%.\n\nTWO QUESTIONS, NEITHER PRE-JUDGED:\n  A. Can a linker that scanned files and emitted nothing distinguish \"the\n     pattern is genuinely absent from this repo\" from \"I was misconfigured or\n     my gate never fired\"? If it can, unreported is the wrong value for it and\n     the derivation should be extended. If it cannot, that is worth declaring\n     positively rather than leaving as an abstention that looks like a gap.\n  B. Is a 1.9s scan of 353 files for a pattern absent from the repo worth an\n     activation gate? This is the cost half of the original INV-bikaj concern,\n     now at 3.2% rather than 15%.\n\nDO NOT close this by reasoning from the 51. A reason derivable from\nfiles_analyzed=0 is not evidence about the 3 that analysed files - that is the\nabsent-versus-empty substitution this project keeps making.\n\nMEASUREMENT PROVENANCE: .hypergumbo/self-analysis.json, generated\n2026-09-16T03:06:42Z, schema 0.20.7, tool 8.0.0. The analysis_runs record key\nis \"pass\", not \"pass_id\"; a probe keyed on pass_id returns None for every run\nand reports every named pass ABSENT, which is a plausible-looking wrong answer\nrather than an error."  # c958
    fields: {}  # c958
- op: discuss  # 89eb
  at: '2026-09-16T19:26:36Z'  # 89eb
  by: agent  # 89eb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 89eb
  clock: 2  # 89eb
  nonce: 89eb  # 89eb
  message: "QUESTION A ANSWERED, AND THE PREMISE OF THIS ITEM'S OWN MEASUREMENT WAS WRONG.\nFixed in PR #1005 (dev db846f196f).\n\nTHE CORRECTION I OWE THIS ITEM. I filed it hours ago at INV-bikaj's closure\nwith the split \"51 no_candidate_files, design-correct / 3 unreported\". EIGHT OF\nTHE 51 WERE FALSE. derive_silence_reason stamps no_candidate_files -- documented\nas \"the pass received zero input files ... the only silence the orchestrator can\nattribute with certainty\" -- whenever files_analyzed == 0. Zero is also the\nAnalysisRun dataclass default, so a linker that read four hundred files and never\nassigned the counter was indistinguishable from one that received no input. The\nitem told the reader not to reason from the 51; the sharper reason is that the\n51 itself was measured on a field that lies.\n\nHOW IT WAS MEASURED, since the static form of this question over-claims and\nunder-claims at once. Path.read_text and Path.read_bytes were patched to\nattribute each read to the calling linker module (stack walk to the nearest\nhypergumbo_core.linkers.* frame) and a full self-survey run. A first probe\npatched read_text only -- a one-of-three instrument that reported the eleven\nread_bytes linkers as reading nothing; a static grep flagged nine and both\nover-claimed (pyffi et al. read 0 on a pure-Python mini corpus) and missed\nwebsocket-linker entirely. Only the two-primitive runtime probe agrees with\nitself across corpora.\n\nTHE EIGHT, all stamped no_candidate_files while reading:\n  annotation-convention  834 files    grpc            397    pyffi          389\n  di-resolution          396          crypto-flow      17    message-dispatch 17\n  solidity-abi            14          wasm-bindgen     14\nThe statically eligible class is larger than the eight that fired here:\nEIGHTEEN linker modules read files and contain no files_analyzed assignment at\nall, so a Vue/Rails/Swift corpus produces more.\n\nANSWER TO A: yes, a linker that scanned files and emitted nothing CAN\ndistinguish \"the construct is absent\" from \"my gate never fired\" -- files_read\n> 0 refutes the second directly, and the pass body knows its own match count.\nBUT THE CAPABILITY IS UNREACHABLE, which is the part worth acting on.\npass_silence documents NO_CANDIDATE_CONSTRUCT as \"only a pass BODY may report\nthis\", and both stamp sites -- linkers/registry.py and analyze/all_analyzers.py\n-- assign silence_reason UNCONDITIONALLY, clobbering anything a body sets. Five\nof the seven declared values (no_candidate_construct, dependency_unavailable,\nbackend_disabled, prerequisite_absent, pass_crashed) have ZERO producers\nanywhere in packages/*/src/. The one-line prerequisite is to guard the stamp the\nway duration_ms is guarded; deciding which of the eleven silent linkers may\nhonestly claim no_candidate_construct is per-body judgment and is NOT\npre-judged here.\n\nTHREE OF THE FIVE PRODUCERLESS VALUES HAVE A FREE-TEXT TWIN ALREADY IN\nPRODUCTION, which is the two-channel defect this item's LIVE note names, now\nlocated in code: a crashing linker goes to Limits.record_crashed_pass ->\nlimits.skipped_passes[].reason (pass_crashed's twin); \"rust-analyzer backend not\nenabled\" is backend_disabled's twin; the grammar-missing prose family is\ndependency_unavailable's. One concept, two channels, and the vocabulary half is\nthe empty one.\n\nANSWER TO B, restated on corrected data. The cohort this item exists to explain\nis not 3 runs / 3734 ms / 3.2%. Post-fix self-survey at tip (97 runs, 207647 ms):\nunreported = 11 runs, 9922 ms, 4.78% of pass time.\n  pyffi 389f/2536ms  graphql-resolver 397f/2167  message-queue 397f/1839\n  annotation-convention 834f/1271  grpc 397f/995  di-resolution 396f/988\n  ipc 8f/40  solidity-abi 14f/27  wasm-bindgen 14f/27  crypto-flow 17f/16\n  message-dispatch 17f/16\nDistribution moved no_candidate_files 51 -> 43, unreported 3 -> 11. Whether\n4.78% is worth an activation gate is the owner's call and is recorded on\nINV-nanon with the census; tightening a gate is the WITHHOLDING direction and\ncan drop real edges silently, so it is surfaced, not performed.\n\nRESIDUAL NOT FIXED, stated rather than implied. The new gate is syntactic and\nscoped to linkers/, and does not check that a body-supplied count is ACCURATE:\nwebsocket-linker reports files_analyzed=2 while reading 405 files, and\nroute-handler-linker deliberately stores a ROUTE count in the same field. That\nis a field-overload defect (one name, two quantities), distinct from the\nfalse-zero fixed here, and unfiled."  # 89eb
